      "title": "Draw one shared altitude",
      "body": "<p>Use the middle side as a base and find its height from the area. Write a Pythagoras equation for each sloping side.</p>",
      "recap": "A perpendicular height creates right triangles whose horizontal lengths and common height relate to the original sides.",
      "pitfall": "The foot need not initially be assumed inside the base; a signed horizontal coordinate avoids that assumption.",
